## 2. Code Quality Review

### Bad Coding Patterns

**1. Dynamic `import()` inside hot controller paths (Critical)**
```js
// hod.controller.js — lines 21, 64, 86
const RoleAssignment = (await import("../Models/roleAssignment.model.js")).default;
```
Dynamic imports are re-evaluated on every request. Node caches them after the first load but the pattern is an anti-pattern here — it creates unnecessary async overhead and makes refactoring hard. Just use a static `import` at the top of the file.

**2. N+1 query risk in `getProgressOverview` (generalOffice.controller.js:54)**
```js
const counts = await Promise.all(
    statuses.map(async (s) => ({
        status: s,
        count: await Application.countDocuments({ status: s }),
    }))
);
```
This fires 10 separate DB queries (one per status). Should use a single aggregation pipeline:
```js
const result = await Application.aggregate([
  { $group: { _id: "$status", count: { $sum: 1 } } }
]);
```

**3. Duplicated pagination boilerplate (4 controllers)**
[admin.controller.js](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/controllers/admin.controller.js), [admissionCell.controller.js](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/controllers/admissionCell.controller.js), [generalOffice.controller.js](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/controllers/generalOffice.controller.js), [accountOffice.controller.js](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/controllers/accountOffice.controller.js), and [hod.controller.js](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/controllers/hod.controller.js) all contain identical pagination logic:
```js
const skip = (parseInt(page) - 1) * parseInt(limit);
const [items, total] = await Promise.all([
    Model.find(filter).skip(skip).limit(parseInt(limit)),
    Model.countDocuments(filter)
]);
```
This should be extracted into a shared `paginate(model, filter, options)` utility.

**4. Duplicated [escapeRegex](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/controllers/admin.controller.js#11-14) function (3 files)**
`admin.controller.js:11`, `generalOffice.controller.js:8`, `hod.controller.js:7` all define their own [escapeRegex](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/controllers/admin.controller.js#11-14). Should live in `utils/`.

**5. Broken schema reference in [application.model.js](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/Models/application.model.js) (line 50)**
```js
identityProof: { type: documentSchema, default: () => ({}) },
```
`documentSchema` is not imported or defined in this file. This will throw a Mongoose schema validation error at startup.

**6. Inconsistent import path casing**
[admin.routes.js](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/Routes/Admin/admin.routes.js) imports from `"../../Controllers/admin.controller.js"` (capital C), while [accountOffice.routes.js](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/Routes/Account_Office/accountOffice.routes.js) imports from `"../../controllers/accountOffice.controller.js"` (lowercase c). On Linux deployments this will cause random `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` crashes.

**7. Unused [User](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/controllers/auth.controller.js#7-18) import in `application.model.js:2`**
```js
import User from "../Models/user.model.js"
```
This is never used inside [application.model.js](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/Models/application.model.js).

**8. [validateRequest](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/utils/validateRequest.js#3-14) utility is defined but never used**
[utils/validateRequest.js](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/utils/validateRequest.js) is exported but not imported in any route or controller file.

### TypeScript Usage

- ❌ **TypeScript is completely absent.** The project description says "TypeScript" but there is no TypeScript anywhere — no `.ts` files, no `tsconfig.json`, no type declarations.
- All models return `any`-typed documents. Without TypeScript, there is no compile-time guarantee that the fields being written to/read from match the schema.

