## 5. Technical Debt

### Architectural Debt

| Debt | Description | Impact |
|---|---|---|
| No TypeScript | All code is plain JS. Type errors, wrong field names, and API shape bugs only show up at runtime | High |
| No service layer | Business logic (create application, match students, verify payment flow) lives in controllers | High |
| No test suite | Zero unit or integration tests | Critical |
| Static file upload via URL | Documents are stored as URLs that are supplied by the client. No actual file upload mechanism exists in the backend | High |
| No API versioning | Breaking changes break all clients | Medium |
| Single [.env](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/.env) for all environments | No environment-specific config, no schema validation | Medium |

### Outdated / Risky Dependencies

| Package | Current | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `express` | `^5.2.1` | Express 5 is still RC/stable-ish but not the LTS version; some ecosystem tools haven't caught up. Not a blocker, but monitor. |
| `dotenv` | `^17.3.1` | Very recent major version — watch for breaking changes. |
| `nodemon` | Listed in `dependencies` (not `devDependencies`) | Dev-only tool shipped with production bundle. Move to `devDependencies`. |
| No `helmet` | Missing | HTTP security headers (HSTS, CSP, X-Frame-Options, etc.) not set |
| No `express-rate-limit` | Missing | No rate limiting on any endpoint |
| No `zod`/`joi` | Missing | No input validation library |
| No test runner | Missing | No `vitest`, `jest`, or similar |

### General Code Maintainability Risks

1. **No `.env.example`** — New developers don't know which env vars are required.
2. **[DETAILED_ANALYSIS.txt](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/DETAILED_ANALYSIS.txt) in repo** — 26KB text file that appears to be internal notes/analysis. Should not be in the repository, especially if it contains architectural decisions or credentials.
3. **[package.json](file:///c:/Users/Varun/Mits/backend/package.json)** has no `"start"` script (only `"dev": "nodemon"`). Production deployments need a `"start": "node index.js"` script.
4. **Typo in `document.model.js:27`**: `"domaicile"` should be `"domicile"`. This will cause mismatches when validating this docType.

