## Backend Architecture Improvement Suggestions

```
backend/                  ← proposed structure
  src/
    api/
      auth/
        auth.routes.ts
        auth.controller.ts
        auth.service.ts        ← new: business logic here
      student/
        student.routes.ts
        student.controller.ts
        student.service.ts
      admin/
        ...
    models/               ← flat, all lowercase
      user.model.ts
      application.model.ts
      document.model.ts
      payment.model.ts
      roleAssignment.model.ts
      studentList.model.ts
    middlewares/
      auth.middleware.ts
      error.middleware.ts
      rateLimiter.middleware.ts  ← new
      validate.middleware.ts     ← new, powered by zod
    utils/
      ApiError.ts
      apiResponse.ts
      asyncHandler.ts
      paginate.ts              ← new
      escapeRegex.ts           ← new
    config/
      db.ts
      env.ts                   ← new: typed env validation with zod
    types/
      express.d.ts             ← new: augment Express Request type
  tests/
    auth.test.ts
    student.test.ts
    ...
  .env
  .env.example              ← new
  .gitignore                ← includes .env
  tsconfig.json             ← new
  package.json
  index.ts
```

### Key Architectural Decisions

| Decision | Recommendation | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Auth strategy | Issue app-signed JWT on Google login | Eliminates per-request Google RTT; allows custom claims |
| Validation | `zod` schemas per endpoint | Type-safe, composable, works with TypeScript |
| File uploads | Presigned URLs from cloud storage (S3, GCS, R2) | Remove client-supplied URL vulnerability; backend never handles bytes |
| Caching | In-memory TTL cache for overview/stats endpoints | 10× performance improvement for read-heavy admin views |
| DB indexes | Add compound index on `{ application: 1 }` for Documents and Payments | Critical for sub-ms query times at scale |
| Rate limiting | `express-rate-limit` on all routes, stricter on `/api/auth` | Prevents abuse |
| Testing | `vitest` + `supertest` + `@faker-js/faker` | Fast, modern, TypeScript-first |
| Logging | `pino` with `pino-http` | Structured JSON logs, excellent performance |
